# shir_nodes/cut_at.node — expression-level semantic IR node.
# CutAt: cut `text` at ONE occurrence of `delim` — the four single-star
# glob-strip identities that are pure find()/rfind() work:
#
#   ${v%%lit*}   keep the head BEFORE the first  occurrence  (head,  first)
#   ${v%lit*}    keep the head BEFORE the last   occurrence  (head,  !first)
#   ${v#*lit}    keep the tail AFTER  the first  occurrence  (!head, first)
#   ${v##*lit}   keep the tail AFTER  the last   occurrence  (!head, !first)
#
# No match leaves the text unchanged (bash's strip is a no-op when the
# pattern does not match). `delim` is a magic-free literal (the fold
# refuses `*`/`?`/`[`/`\` bodies): `is_magic_free`.
#
# The identities are THEOREMS, not an appeal to glob semantics:
# docs/fm/TextOps/ShIR_TextOps_Cut.thy proves `find_first`/`rfind_last`
# (a returned index is an occurrence, none means no occurrence anywhere,
# leftmost/maximal) and, over arbitrary text and literal, `cut_at_sound`
# (each form is take/drop at its own occurrence, text unchanged on no
# match) and `affix_strip_fold_sound` (the fold's contract: all four star
# shapes at those primitives, plus the plain branch at either end —
# `#lit*` is AffixStrip's strip_prefix, `%*lit` its strip_suffix, the
# latter via `cut_head_last_at_trail`).
# PATTERN SIDE, now proved for the fragment: ShIR_TextOps_Glob models shell
# patterns as PLit/PAny/PStar with matcher `pmatch`, and proves that the
# shortest-match strip of `lit*` is exactly the FIRST occurrence of the
# literal (TextOps#strip_pre_lit_star: `strip_pre [PLit p, PStar] t` = drop at
# the first occurrence, identity on a miss). So the `#*lit` arm's
# "shortest match" is a theorem about a glob matcher, not a reading of bash.
# BOUNDARY, exact: both extrema are now modelled over the same `pseg` semantics, so the
# longest arms are theorems, not an appeal to `rfind`. Over that matcher, for the four
# star shapes of this node:
#   ${v##*lit}  longest   = the tail after the LAST occurrence   strip_pre_long_star_lit
#   ${v%%lit*}  longest   = the head before the FIRST occurrence strip_suf_long_lit_star
#   ${v%lit*}   shortest  = the head before the LAST occurrence  strip_suf_short_lit_star
#   ${v#*lit}   shortest  = the tail after the FIRST occurrence strip_pre_lit_star
# each with the no-match arm the text unchanged, each (TextOps#-prefixed) over an
# arbitrary text and literal. "Longest" and "shortest" are two extrema of ONE match set
# (`pre_ok` / `suf_at`), not two primitives: TextOps#strip_pre_long_star_lit is the
# `Max` of the prefix match positions and TextOps#strip_pre_lit_star its `Min`, and
# TextOps#shortest_is_not_the_longest / TextOps#trailing_shortest_is_not_the_longest
# refute collapsing them, while TextOps#greedy_star_is_not_the_last_separator_strip
# refutes the greedy "a star strips everything" reading. The `lit*` prefix form is
# decided separately because its longest match is the whole text:
# TextOps#strip_pre_long_lit_star. The whole-text case is TextOps#strip_pre_long_star
# and TextOps#strip_pre_long_star_lit_whole.
# Character classes, ranges, negation, extglob, brace alternation and quoting are
# outside the fragment altogether (TextOps#fragment_is_three_constructors and the
# one-byte tests); the fold refuses magic bodies, so no lowering reaches the node with
# one. An empty `delim` never reaches this node — the fold special-cases it — and
# `cut_at_empty_pattern` proves why: with `[]` the two primitives match at different
# indices, so the four arms split ([] / s / s / []) and no single node describes the
# case. The empty-literal form is itself decided by the longest laws
# (TextOps#last_occurrence_witness).
#
# Emitted by the `affix-strip-fold` transform (the star-form branch; the
# plain-literal branch keeps using AffixStrip).
#
# Backends: Rust (find/rfind + slicing), C (one strstr find + a vbuf
#   copy — see c_backend's ext_value_c CutAt arm) — target-gated offers;
#   other backends accept by adding a render arm and their target to the
#   gate (the FieldGrab offer pattern).
# Fallback: sh2.cutAt(text, delim, head, first)

node CutAt
tag "CutAt"
kind expr
# storage_class str_bounded
field text: expr
field delim: string
field head: bool
field first: bool
spec: TextOps#cut_at_sound
spec: TextOps#strip_pre_long_star_lit
spec: TextOps#strip_pre_long_lit_star
spec: TextOps#strip_suf_long_star_lit
spec: TextOps#strip_suf_short_lit_star
